# Internal telemetry planning/ops docs (legal-risk notes, read-token architecture,
# private vault paths, backend source) — not for the public repo. All of these
# were untracked with `git rm --cached` before the v0.2.1 release; they remain on
# disk. TELEMETRY.md is the public contract — these are the internals behind it.
# NOTE: a blanket `specs/` rule was tried and reverted — git cannot re-include a
# file once a parent directory is excluded, so this is scoped per-file instead.
specs/telemetry/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
specs/telemetry/LITE_PLAN.md
specs/telemetry/apps_script/Code.gs
specs/telemetry/apps_script/GithubTraffic.gs
specs/telemetry/apps_script/RepairGithubTraffic.gs
specs/telemetry/dashboard/DESIGN.md
specs/telemetry/dashboard/DATA_FLOW.md
specs/telemetry/dashboard/build_dashboard.py

# Internal telemetry status docs — untracked; keep out of the next `git add -A`.
# Being gitignored does not hide these from the owner on disk — it only keeps
# them out of the commit/publish path, which is the point.
specs/telemetry/MEETING_UPDATE.md
specs/telemetry/data_workflow_overview.png
specs/telemetry/MERGE_MANIFEST.md

# Telemetry dashboard output — contains opt-in feedback PII, local-only, never commit
specs/telemetry/dashboard/dashboard.html
